From c1d37bdda855827c1e8ad2aebe3eb9e542597819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Hainke <vincent@systemli.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] interface: fix the DNS filters for VLAN tagged packets

For a packet with a single VLAN tag, the kernel removes the tag from
the packet data before the ingress filters run, but tc still matches
the packet with protocol 802.1Q. The filters for VLAN tagged DNS
replies therefore see the IP header at offset 0, like the filters
without a tag. 'offset plus 4' doesn't move the matches, it only
applies to linked filters, which is why the IPv4 filter worked anyway.

The IPv6 filter was added with protocol ipv6 instead of 802.1Q, so it
only repeated the filter before it, and DNS replies over IPv6 with a
VLAN tag were never redirected. The IPv4 filter didn't check the IP
version and took IPv6 packets with 00 35 at that offset of the source
address for DNS replies, and it took fragments for DNS replies like
the filter fixed in the previous commit.

Match the IP version in both filters, use protocol 802.1Q for IPv6,
only take IPv4 packets with a fragment offset of 0, and drop the
offset which had no effect. Packets with two VLAN tags need separate
filters for the inner tag, they follow in the next commit.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Nick Hainke <vincent@systemli.org>
---
 interface.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/interface.c b/interface.c
index 141051a..46048e6 100644
--- a/interface.c
+++ b/interface.c
@@ -379,8 +379,14 @@ cmd_add_ingress(struct qosify_iface *iface, bool eth)
 			 "flowid 1:1 action mirred egress redirect dev " QOSIFY_DNS_IFNAME);
 	qosify_run_cmd(buf, false);
 
+	/*
+	 * With a VLAN tag, tc matches the VLAN protocol, but the tag is no
+	 * longer in the packet data, so the offsets are the same as without
+	 * it. The VLAN can carry IPv4 and IPv6, check the IP version.
+	 */
 	ofs = prepare_filter_cmd(buf, sizeof(buf), iface->ifname, prio++, true, false);
-	APPEND(buf, ofs, " protocol 802.1Q u32 offset plus 4 match ip sport 53 0xffff "
+	APPEND(buf, ofs, " protocol 802.1Q u32 match u8 0x40 0xf0 at 0 "
+			 "match ip sport 53 0xffff match u16 0 0x1fff at 6 "
 			 "flowid 1:1 action mirred egress redirect dev " QOSIFY_DNS_IFNAME);
 	qosify_run_cmd(buf, false);
 
@@ -390,7 +396,8 @@ cmd_add_ingress(struct qosify_iface *iface, bool eth)
 	qosify_run_cmd(buf, false);
 
 	ofs = prepare_filter_cmd(buf, sizeof(buf), iface->ifname, prio++, true, false);
-	APPEND(buf, ofs, " protocol ipv6 u32 offset plus 4 match ip6 sport 53 0xffff "
+	APPEND(buf, ofs, " protocol 802.1Q u32 match u8 0x60 0xf0 at 0 "
+			 "match ip6 sport 53 0xffff "
 			 "flowid 1:1 action mirred egress redirect dev " QOSIFY_DNS_IFNAME);
 	qosify_run_cmd(buf, false);
 
